The failure is now isolated to the one POSIX-form link target (`../bin/go`): Windows creates the link, but its resolver rejects that stored separator form. The clean adapter boundary is to materialize the target with native path components, verify the native link still denotes the vector target, and project only `readlink`’s native separators back to the vector’s protocol bytes while the real product fingerprinting and link validation run unchanged. I’m implementing that narrow mapping and strengthening its regression assertion.
